      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(exec): require approval for OpenClaw lifecycle commands",
        "body": "﻿Fixes #99518\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where exec commands through gateway or node hosts could let OpenClaw gateway/daemon lifecycle mutations pass through normal allowlist or auto-review paths when they should require explicit approval.\n\nThe affected workflow is OpenClaw self-management from exec surfaces: stopping, starting, restarting, running, deleting, or uninstalling the gateway/daemon through CLI, launchctl, systemctl, schtasks, process-kill, shell-wrapper, package-manager, Windows shim, `env -S`, `xargs`/`find`, `sudo`/`doas`, and dispatch-wrapper commands.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a focused lifecycle classifier to the exec approval policy and wires it into the main gateway-host, node-host, and direct `system.run` approval paths. The guard forces explicit approval for OpenClaw lifecycle mutations unless exec is already in yolo mode (`security=full`, `ask=off`).\n\nForeground gateway runtime forms such as `openclaw gateway`, `openclaw gateway run`, `openclaw gateway restart`, and `openclaw gateway --force restart` are treated as lifecycle mutations. Read-only inspection remains outside the guard, including `openclaw gateway status`, `openclaw gateway --help`, `openclaw gateway run --help`, `launchctl print`, `systemctl status`, `schtasks /Query`, and generic read-only process lookups. `openclaw gateway call` is method-aware: lifecycle RPCs such as `update.run` and `gateway.restart.request` require explicit lifecycle approval, while read-only RPCs such as `health`, `update.status`, and `logs.tail` do not.\n\nThe classifier also handles lifecycle commands hidden behind common command carriers, including nested `env`, `env -S`, shell wrappers, package runners, `find`/`xargs`, process-kill pipelines, known environment expansions, unknown partial environments that could expand to OpenClaw, and Node launcher forms without treating benign `node -e` / `node --print` script arguments as executable paths. The classifier remains out of `openclaw/plugin-sdk/infra-runtime`; the deprecated SDK shim now explicitly preserves the previous exec approval exports without exposing this internal lifecycle taxonomy as plugin API.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators get an extra human confirmation before an agent or auto-review path can stop, start, restart, run, delete, or uninstall the OpenClaw gateway/daemon in non-yolo configurations. Existing yolo-mode behavior, read-only status/query commands, and public plugin SDK export counts are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFinal branch head validated: `c1d8b304fd6cfb148b58c87e5da13740341117ae`.\n\nBefore/source proof: current `main` only hard-gated the existing security-audit suppression case before generic ask/allowlist/auto-review handling. OpenClaw lifecycle mutations were not classified before durable allowlist or auto-review decisions in the gateway-host, node-host, or direct `system.run` paths.\n\nAfter-fix direct classifier proof on this head, importing the production `commandRequiresOpenClawLifecycleApproval` function and parsing each command through the same shell-argv splitter used by the policy:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"branchHead\": \"c1d8b304fd\",\n  \"results\": [\n    { \"label\": \"gateway force restart\", \"command\": \"openclaw gateway --force restart\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": true },\n    { \"label\": \"gateway run port\", \"command\": \"openclaw gateway run --port 18889\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": true },\n    { \"label\": \"gateway lifecycle rpc\", \"command\": \"openclaw gateway call update.run --params '{}'\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": true },\n    { \"label\": \"gateway readonly rpc\", \"command\": \"openclaw gateway call update.status\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": false },\n    { \"label\": \"deep env lifecycle\", \"command\": \"env env env env env openclaw gateway restart\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": true },\n    { \"label\": \"env-S lifecycle\", \"command\": \"env -S 'openclaw gateway --force restart'\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": true },\n    { \"label\": \"shell env lifecycle\", \"command\": \"env CMD=openclaw sh -c '$CMD gateway restart'\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": true },\n    { \"label\": \"package runner lifecycle\", \"command\": \"npx openclaw@latest -- gateway restart\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": true },\n    { \"label\": \"process kill pipeline\", \"command\": \"pidof openclaw | xargs kill\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": true },\n    { \"label\": \"node eval argv\", \"command\": \"node -e 'console.log(process.argv)' openclaw gateway restart\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": false },\n    { \"label\": \"readonly status\", \"command\": \"openclaw status --all\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": false },\n    { \"label\": \"systemctl status\", \"command\": \"systemctl --type service status openclaw-gateway.service\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": false },\n    { \"label\": \"systemctl lifecycle signal\", \"command\": \"systemctl --signal=TERM kill openclaw-gateway.service\", \"requiresLifecycleApproval\": true }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nEarlier isolated gateway-host proof exercised the runtime approval path with `openclaw gateway --force`: an isolated branch gateway was healthy, the lifecycle command returned a blocking `approval-unavailable` result before execution, `autoReviewCalls` stayed `0`, and yolo mode (`security=full`, `ask=off`) still passed through without the lifecycle warning. Later follow-ups expanded classifier coverage; the final head revalidated the host/runtime approval surfaces with the focused tests below.\n\nFocused tests on final head:\n\n```shell\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/exec-approvals-policy.test.ts --testNamePattern=\"OpenClaw lifecycle|env -S|SHELL|xargs|find|openclaw update|--update|uninstall|openclaw@|pnpm dlx openclaw --|OC_BIN|update.run|update.status|dry-run|partial environments|complete|read-only or generic|eval|deeply nested transparent carriers|gateway --force restart|gateway --port 18789 restart|pidof openclaw|pgrep -f openclaw|unknown POSIX plus|carries env assignments|node -e|node --print|node -r\"\n# Tests  261 passed | 85 skipped (346)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-gateway.test.ts --testNamePattern=\"OpenClaw lifecycle|gateway lifecycle RPC|durable allowlist\"\n# Tests  5 passed | 53 skipped (58)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-node.test.ts --testNamePattern=\"OpenClaw lifecycle\"\n# Tests  1 passed | 48 skipped (49)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/node-host/invoke-system-run.test.ts --testNamePattern=\"OpenClaw lifecycle|empty env operands\"\n# Tests  2 passed | 33 skipped (35)\n```\n\nSDK surface report on final head:\n\n```shell\nnode scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.mjs --check\n# passed\n# public package SDK entrypoints: exports 10421, callable exports 5233\n# infra-runtime budget restored to 585; the lifecycle classifier is not public plugin SDK surface\n# public wildcard reexports: 213\n```\n\nStatic/type checks on final head:\n\n```shell\nnode scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo\n# passed\n\nnode scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.extensions.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/extensions.tsbuildinfo\n# passed\n\n$files = git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD; node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs @files\n# passed\n\ngit diff --check\n# passed\n```\n\nAutoreview note: branch autoreview was clean on the previous `e43e1f19b6` head before the SDK shim repair. After the SDK shim repair on this final head, the local autoreview helper was attempted again but was blocked by a Codex usage-limit error before returning review findings, so this PR does not claim a clean local autoreview result for `c1d8b304fd`. The latest ClawSweeper re-review is the authoritative reviewer for this final head.\n\nProof limitation: the final proof covers the main gateway-host, node-host, and direct `system.run` exec approval paths touched by this PR. It does not claim to redesign unrelated plugin SDK/app-server auto-review surfaces.\r\n",
